-- title:
--   Definitions for On singular perturbations of quantum dynamical semigroups
-- statement:
--   The objects the formalized statements of *On singular perturbations of quantum dynamical semigroups* (arXiv:1706.04866) are stated in. Each was checked against the paper by a blind read-back and a moderator.
--
--   - `halfLineMeasure`: PDF p.3: Lebesgue measure on the half-line; including its endpoint changes no Lp class.
--   - `HalfLine`: PDF pp.3,7: the actual infinite-dimensional complex L2 space.
--   - `Evolution`: PDF p.1: normal CP subunital evolutions on the full bounded-operator algebra.
--   - `TraceEvolution`: PDF pp.1,3: trace-norm predual evolution. The chosen basis only writes the trace.
--   - `identityObservable`: PDF p.1: the identity observable.
--   - `IsPredual`: PDF pp.1–2: actual preadjoint duality, including trace-norm orbit continuity. Continuity is expressed by the nuclear norm on differences of trace-class operators.
--   - `InDualGeneratorGraph`: PDF pp.3–4: the full ultraweak generator graph, tested by every trace-class input. This is not the operator-norm derivative of the observable orbit.
--   - `dualGeneratorDomain`: PDF p.4: full ultraweak generator domain.
--   - `domainAlgebra`: PDF p.4: all three memberships in Arveson's domain algebra.
--   - `IsNonunitalStarDomain`: PDF p.5: a complex star algebra without requiring an identity element.
--   - `IsLeftShift`: PDF p.3: exact left translation on L2 equivalence classes, for each time and vector.
--   - `IsShiftPair`: PDF pp.3–4, (6): the actual two shift evolutions and their predual relationship.
--   - `LocallyAC`: PDF pp.3,7: absolute continuity on each compact half-line interval.
--   - `H1Trace`: PDF p.3: the full H1 derivative graph with its genuine boundary trace. The endpoint is evaluated only on a locally absolutely continuous representative.
--   - `h1Domain`: PDF p.3: H1 has no imposed zero boundary condition.
--   - `DirichletTriple`: PDF p.7: the full Dirichlet H2 graph. The first derivative has a finite boundary trace but is not required to vanish there.
--   - `dirichletDomain`: PDF p.7: H2 intersect H1_0, on the actual L2 space.
--   - `closureGraph`: PDF pp.1–2: the closed graph generated by K on the proposed common core.
--   - `SolvesCore`: PDF p.2, (3): the backward equation for a countable family of jumps. Summability is explicit, so the infinite sum never uses a divergent-series default.
--   - `StandardRepresentation`: PDF p.2: every admissible common invariant core and every contraction generator. Maximal accretivity is expressed by the range characterization on the closed graph. The core need not equal the full generator domain.
--   - `IsStandard`: PDF p.2: existence over ALL admissible K,L_j,D, not one fixed differential expression.
--   - `IsFullRepresentation`: PDF p.9: inside the contradiction lemmas only, K is taken on its full closed domain.
--   - `SolvesDiffusion`: PDF p.7, (15): the specific Dirichlet diffusion equation; both drift signs are positive because the Hilbert operator is K=-d²/dx².
--   - `IsAbsorbingDiffusion`: PDF p.7: the actual minimal absorbing diffusion, characterized without assuming any asserted generator-domain description or heat-kernel formula.
--   - `IsLossReset`: PDF pp.3,8: the rank-one reset on the full actual generator domain. No value of its ambient totalization outside that domain is used.
--   - `IsResetConstruction`: PDF pp.3–4,8–9: the source's minimal resolvent-series perturbation, not an arbitrary semigroup with a stipulated generator domain.
--   - `ResetGeneratorFormula`: PDF pp.3–4,8–9, (7),(19),(20): the equality of full actual generator graphs.
--   - `IsNuclearDiagonal`: PDF pp.3,8,11: nuclear diagonal density, as an L1 equivalence class. Only its continuous or differentiable representatives may be evaluated at zero.
--   - `HasDiagonalBoundary`: PDF p.4: the diagonal boundary value, using a continuous boundary representative.
--   - `HasBoundaryFlux`: PDF pp.8–9,11: the right derivative of the diagonal trace density at the absorbing endpoint.
--   - `HasKernel`: PDF pp.3,6,7: an actual L2 integral kernel, with integrability of every operator action. Equality of kernels is always equality almost everywhere for product Lebesgue measure.
--   - `characteristicPoint`: PDF pp.11–12: r=min(x,y), v=x-y parametrize each characteristic from its boundary.
--   - `CharacteristicFirst`: PDF pp.3,6–7, Proposition 1: local characteristic AC and its actual weak derivative. There is no zero boundary condition. The parameter v ranges over the whole real line.
--   - `CharacteristicSecond`: PDF pp.13–14, Proposition 9, corrected using its proof: zero at r=0 on each characteristic, rather than zero at every interior point. No zero first-derivative boundary condition is imposed. Both regularity clauses are local.
--   - `IsReboundDecomposition`: PDF p.4: an arbitrary countable rebound factorization; zero padding is permitted.
--   - `boundaryJumpGraph`: PDF p.4: the actual, possibly nonclosable, H1 boundary-jump graph in L2 times L2.
--   - `IsNonclosableGraph`: PDF p.4: nonclosability means that the graph closure is not single-valued at zero.
--   - `reflectedWeight`: PDF p.12, (30): the reflected heat weight is a DIFFERENCE, with squared absolute values.
--   - `heatKernel`: PDF p.12, (30): used only for t>0, with integrability separately asserted.
--   - `TracePathContinuous`: PDF pp.11–13: trace-norm continuity of a full complex trace-class trajectory.
--   - `WeakForwardCauchy`: PDF pp.11–13, (27): the weak forward Cauchy problem on every Dirichlet H2 test pair, including the prescribed initial datum. There is no positivity restriction on the datum.
--   - `heatRegion`: PDF pp.11–13: the positive time/interior characteristic region.
--   - `ClassicalHeatSection`: PDF pp.11–13, (29): classical heat regularity in (t,r) on one characteristic. Here r=(u-|v|)/2, so the equation dt=ddr is exactly partial_t=4 partial_u². No regularity in the transverse parameter v is required.
--   - `HeatCauchy`: PDF pp.12–13, Proposition 8: a jointly measurable kernel version, classical along almost every characteristic, with the same trace-norm initial condition. All operator kernel actions carry their integrability conditions through HasKernel.
-- source:
--   On singular perturbations of quantum dynamical semigroups, arXiv:1706.04866v5, https://arxiv.org/abs/1706.04866v5

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_QAlgorithms_Papers_Independent_Dependency50_P13
import Definitions.Def_QAlgorithms_Papers_Independent_Claimed50_P50
import Definitions.Def_QAlgorithms_Papers_Independent_Next46_P09

/-!
Holevo, On singular perturbations of quantum dynamical semigroups,
arXiv:1706.04866v5. Paper-local definitions use the full nuclear trace class
and actual right-derivative generator graphs. The minimal evolutions are
specified by their weak master equations and CP minimality, never by their
claimed generator domains. Construction assertions are included in the two
headline construction theorems. Compilation is pending the batch handoff.
-/

noncomputable section

open Filter MeasureTheory
open scoped BigOperators ENNReal

namespace QAlgorithms.Papers.Independent.Renew46.P06

open QAlgorithms.Papers.Independent.Dependency50.P13
  (TraceClass State NuclearRepresentation traceNormValue operatorTrace)
open QAlgorithms.Papers.Independent.Claimed50.P50
  (ContractionSemigroup DynamicalSemigroup IsCPOnBoundedOperators
    IsUnitalQDS IsRelaxingEvolution)
open QAlgorithms.Papers.Independent.Next46.P09
  (TraceDynamicalSemigroup InTraceGeneratorGraph TraceGeneratorDomain
    DomainPerturbation IsMinimalPerturbation)

/-- PDF p.3: Lebesgue measure on the half-line; including its endpoint changes no Lp class. -/
def halfLineMeasure : Measure ℝ := volume.restrict (Set.Ioi 0)

/-- PDF pp.3,7: the actual infinite-dimensional complex L2 space. -/
abbrev HalfLine := Lp ℂ 2 halfLineMeasure

/-- PDF p.1: normal CP subunital evolutions on the full bounded-operator algebra. -/
abbrev Evolution := DynamicalSemigroup HalfLine

/-- PDF pp.1,3: trace-norm predual evolution. The chosen basis only writes the trace. -/
abbrev TraceEvolution (b : HilbertBasis ℕ ℂ HalfLine) := TraceDynamicalSemigroup b

/-- PDF p.1: the identity observable. -/
def identityObservable : (HalfLine →L[ℂ] HalfLine) := ContinuousLinearMap.id ℂ HalfLine

/-- PDF pp.1–2: actual preadjoint duality, including trace-norm orbit continuity.
Continuity is expressed by the nuclear norm on differences of trace-class operators. -/
def IsPredual (b : HilbertBasis ℕ ℂ HalfLine) (S : TraceEvolution b)
    (T : Evolution) : Prop :=
  (∀ t rho X, operatorTrace b ((S.maps t rho).val.comp X) = operatorTrace b (rho.val.comp (T.maps t X))) ∧
  (∀ (t : NNReal) (rho : (TraceClass HalfLine)),
    Tendsto (fun s : NNReal => traceNormValue ((S.maps s rho).val - (S.maps t rho).val))
      (nhds t) (nhds 0))

/-- PDF pp.3–4: the full ultraweak generator graph, tested by every trace-class input.
This is not the operator-norm derivative of the observable orbit. -/
def InDualGeneratorGraph (b : HilbertBasis ℕ ℂ HalfLine) (T : Evolution)
    (X Y : (HalfLine →L[ℂ] HalfLine)) : Prop :=
  ∀ rho : (TraceClass HalfLine),
    Tendsto (fun t : ℝ => (t : ℂ)⁻¹ *
      (operatorTrace b (rho.val.comp (T.maps t.toNNReal X)) - operatorTrace b (rho.val.comp X)))
      (nhdsWithin 0 (Set.Ioi 0)) (nhds (operatorTrace b (rho.val.comp Y)))

/-- PDF p.4: full ultraweak generator domain. -/
def dualGeneratorDomain (b : HilbertBasis ℕ ℂ HalfLine) (T : Evolution) : Set (HalfLine →L[ℂ] HalfLine) :=
  {X | ∃ Y, InDualGeneratorGraph b T X Y}

/-- PDF p.4: all three memberships in Arveson's domain algebra. -/
def domainAlgebra (b : HilbertBasis ℕ ℂ HalfLine) (T : Evolution) : Set (HalfLine →L[ℂ] HalfLine) :=
  {X | X ∈ dualGeneratorDomain b T ∧
    X.adjoint.comp X ∈ dualGeneratorDomain b T ∧
    X.comp X.adjoint ∈ dualGeneratorDomain b T}

/-- PDF p.5: a complex star algebra without requiring an identity element. -/
def IsNonunitalStarDomain (A : Set (HalfLine →L[ℂ] HalfLine)) : Prop :=
  (0 : (HalfLine →L[ℂ] HalfLine)) ∈ A ∧
  (∀ X ∈ A, ∀ Y ∈ A, X + Y ∈ A) ∧
  (∀ c : ℂ, ∀ X ∈ A, c • X ∈ A) ∧
  (∀ X ∈ A, X.adjoint ∈ A) ∧
  (∀ X ∈ A, ∀ Y ∈ A, X.comp Y ∈ A) ∧
  identityObservable ∉ A

/-- PDF p.3: exact left translation on L2 equivalence classes, for each time and vector. -/
def IsLeftShift (W : ContractionSemigroup HalfLine) : Prop :=
  ∀ (t : NNReal) (f : HalfLine), ∀ᵐ x : ℝ ∂halfLineMeasure,
    W.maps t f x = f (x + (t : ℝ))

/-- PDF pp.3–4, (6): the actual two shift evolutions and their predual relationship. -/
def IsShiftPair (b : HilbertBasis ℕ ℂ HalfLine) (W : ContractionSemigroup HalfLine)
    (S : TraceEvolution b) (T : Evolution) : Prop :=
  IsPredual b S T ∧ IsRelaxingEvolution W T ∧
  ∀ t rho, (S.maps t rho).val = (W.maps t).comp (rho.val.comp (W.maps t).adjoint)

/-- PDF pp.3,7: absolute continuity on each compact half-line interval. -/
def LocallyAC (f : ℝ → ℂ) : Prop :=
  ∀ R : ℝ, 0 ≤ R → AbsolutelyContinuousOnInterval f 0 R

/-- PDF p.3: the full H1 derivative graph with its genuine boundary trace.
The endpoint is evaluated only on a locally absolutely continuous representative. -/
def H1Trace (f df : HalfLine) (a : ℂ) : Prop :=
  ∃ F : ℝ → ℂ, (F =ᵐ[halfLineMeasure] f) ∧ LocallyAC F ∧ F 0 = a ∧
    (∀ᵐ x : ℝ ∂halfLineMeasure, HasDerivAt F (df x) x)

/-- PDF p.3: H1 has no imposed zero boundary condition. -/
def h1Domain : Set HalfLine := {f | ∃ df a, H1Trace f df a}

/-- PDF p.7: the full Dirichlet H2 graph. The first derivative has a finite
boundary trace but is not required to vanish there. -/
def DirichletTriple (f df ddf : HalfLine) : Prop :=
  ∃ F F1 : ℝ → ℂ,
    (F =ᵐ[halfLineMeasure] f) ∧ (F1 =ᵐ[halfLineMeasure] df) ∧
    F 0 = 0 ∧ LocallyAC F1 ∧
    (∀ x : ℝ, 0 ≤ x → HasDerivWithinAt F (F1 x) (Set.Ici 0) x) ∧
    (∀ᵐ x : ℝ ∂halfLineMeasure, HasDerivAt F1 (ddf x) x)

/-- PDF p.7: H2 intersect H1_0, on the actual L2 space. -/
def dirichletDomain : Set HalfLine := {f | ∃ df ddf, DirichletTriple f df ddf}

/-- PDF pp.1–2: the closed graph generated by K on the proposed common core. -/
def closureGraph {D : Submodule ℂ HalfLine} (K : D →ₗ[ℂ] HalfLine) : Set (HalfLine × HalfLine) :=
  closure {z | ∃ f : D, z = ((f : HalfLine), K f)}

/-- PDF p.2, (3): the backward equation for a countable family of jumps.
Summability is explicit, so the infinite sum never uses a divergent-series default. -/
def SolvesCore (T : Evolution) (D : Submodule ℂ HalfLine)
    (K : D →ₗ[ℂ] HalfLine) (L : ℕ → D →ₗ[ℂ] HalfLine) : Prop :=
  ∀ (t : NNReal) (X : (HalfLine →L[ℂ] HalfLine)) (f g : D),
    Summable (fun j => inner ℂ (L j f) (T.maps t X (L j g))) ∧
    HasDerivWithinAt
      (fun s : ℝ => inner ℂ (f : HalfLine) (T.maps s.toNNReal X (g : HalfLine)))
      ((∑' j, inner ℂ (L j f) (T.maps t X (L j g))) -
        inner ℂ (K f) (T.maps t X (g : HalfLine)) -
        inner ℂ (f : HalfLine) (T.maps t X (K g)))
      (Set.Ici 0) (t : ℝ)

/-- PDF p.2: every admissible common invariant core and every contraction generator.
Maximal accretivity is expressed by the range characterization on the closed graph.
The core need not equal the full generator domain. -/
structure StandardRepresentation (T : Evolution) where
  D : Submodule ℂ HalfLine
  K : D →ₗ[ℂ] HalfLine
  L : ℕ → D →ₗ[ℂ] HalfLine
  C : ContractionSemigroup HalfLine
  dense : Dense (D : Set HalfLine)
  singleValued : ∀ y : HalfLine, (0, y) ∈ closureGraph K → y = 0
  accretive : ∀ z ∈ closureGraph K, 0 ≤ (inner ℂ z.1 z.2).re
  maximal : ∀ lambda : ℝ, 0 < lambda → ∀ f : HalfLine,
    ∃ z ∈ closureGraph K, (lambda : ℂ) • z.1 + z.2 = f
  generates : ∀ x y : HalfLine, (x, y) ∈ closureGraph K ↔
    Tendsto (fun t : ℝ => (t : ℂ)⁻¹ • (C.maps t.toNNReal x - x))
      (nhdsWithin 0 (Set.Ioi 0)) (nhds (-y))
  invariant : ∀ t (f : D), C.maps t (f : HalfLine) ∈ D
  summableLoss : ∀ f : D, Summable (fun j => ‖L j f‖ ^ 2)
  dissipative : ∀ f : D, (∑' j, ‖L j f‖ ^ 2) ≤
    2 * (inner ℂ (f : HalfLine) (K f)).re
  solves : SolvesCore T D K L
  minimal : ∀ U : Evolution, SolvesCore U D K L →
    ∀ t, IsCPOnBoundedOperators (fun X => U.maps t X - T.maps t X)

/-- PDF p.2: existence over ALL admissible K,L_j,D, not one fixed differential expression. -/
def IsStandard (T : Evolution) : Prop := Nonempty (StandardRepresentation T)

/-- PDF p.9: inside the contradiction lemmas only, K is taken on its full closed domain. -/
def IsFullRepresentation {T : Evolution} (R : StandardRepresentation T) : Prop :=
  IsClosed {z : HalfLine × HalfLine | ∃ f : R.D, z = ((f : HalfLine), R.K f)}

/-- PDF p.7, (15): the specific Dirichlet diffusion equation; both drift signs are positive
because the Hilbert operator is K=-d²/dx². -/
def SolvesDiffusion (T : Evolution) : Prop :=
  ∀ (f df ddf g dg ddg : HalfLine),
    DirichletTriple f df ddf → DirichletTriple g dg ddg →
    ∀ (t : NNReal) (X : (HalfLine →L[ℂ] HalfLine)),
      HasDerivWithinAt (fun s : ℝ => inner ℂ f (T.maps s.toNNReal X g))
        (2 * inner ℂ df (T.maps t X dg) + inner ℂ ddf (T.maps t X g) +
          inner ℂ f (T.maps t X ddg)) (Set.Ici 0) (t : ℝ)

/-- PDF p.7: the actual minimal absorbing diffusion, characterized without assuming
any asserted generator-domain description or heat-kernel formula. -/
def IsAbsorbingDiffusion (T : Evolution) : Prop :=
  SolvesDiffusion T ∧ ∀ U : Evolution, SolvesDiffusion U →
    ∀ t, IsCPOnBoundedOperators (fun X => U.maps t X - T.maps t X)

/-- PDF pp.3,8: the rank-one reset on the full actual generator domain.
No value of its ambient totalization outside that domain is used. -/
def IsLossReset (b : HilbertBasis ℕ ℂ HalfLine) (Szero : TraceEvolution b)
    (Omega : State b) (P : DomainPerturbation Szero) : Prop :=
  ∀ rho eta : (TraceClass HalfLine), InTraceGeneratorGraph Szero rho eta →
    (P.maps rho).val = -(operatorTrace b eta.val) • Omega.val.val

/-- PDF pp.3–4,8–9: the source's minimal resolvent-series perturbation, not an arbitrary
semigroup with a stipulated generator domain. -/
def IsResetConstruction (b : HilbertBasis ℕ ℂ HalfLine) (Szero : TraceEvolution b)
    (Omega : State b) (P : DomainPerturbation Szero)
    (S : TraceEvolution b) (T : Evolution) : Prop :=
  IsLossReset b Szero Omega P ∧ IsMinimalPerturbation Szero P S ∧ IsPredual b S T

/-- PDF pp.3–4,8–9, (7),(19),(20): the equality of full actual generator graphs. -/
def ResetGeneratorFormula (b : HilbertBasis ℕ ℂ HalfLine)
    (Szero S : TraceEvolution b) (Omega : State b) : Prop :=
  ∀ rho eta : (TraceClass HalfLine),
    InTraceGeneratorGraph S rho eta ↔
      ∃ etaZero : (TraceClass HalfLine), InTraceGeneratorGraph Szero rho etaZero ∧
        eta.val = etaZero.val - (operatorTrace b etaZero.val) • Omega.val.val

/-- PDF pp.3,8,11: nuclear diagonal density, as an L1 equivalence class.
Only its continuous or differentiable representatives may be evaluated at zero. -/
def IsNuclearDiagonal (rho : (TraceClass HalfLine)) (d : ℝ → ℂ) : Prop :=
  Integrable d halfLineMeasure ∧ ∃ u v : ℕ → HalfLine,
    NuclearRepresentation rho.val u v ∧
      (∀ᵐ x : ℝ ∂halfLineMeasure,
        Summable (fun j => u j x * star (v j x)) ∧
          d x = ∑' j, u j x * star (v j x))

/-- PDF p.4: the diagonal boundary value, using a continuous boundary representative. -/
def HasDiagonalBoundary (rho : (TraceClass HalfLine)) (a : ℂ) : Prop :=
  ∃ d : ℝ → ℂ, IsNuclearDiagonal rho d ∧
    ContinuousWithinAt d (Set.Ici 0) 0 ∧ d 0 = a

/-- PDF pp.8–9,11: the right derivative of the diagonal trace density at the absorbing endpoint. -/
def HasBoundaryFlux (rho : (TraceClass HalfLine)) (a : ℂ) : Prop :=
  ∃ d : ℝ → ℂ, IsNuclearDiagonal rho d ∧ d 0 = 0 ∧
    HasDerivWithinAt d a (Set.Ici 0) 0

/-- PDF pp.3,6,7: an actual L2 integral kernel, with integrability of every operator action.
Equality of kernels is always equality almost everywhere for product Lebesgue measure. -/
def HasKernel (rho : (TraceClass HalfLine)) (k : ℝ × ℝ → ℂ) : Prop :=
  MemLp k 2 (halfLineMeasure.prod halfLineMeasure) ∧
    ∀ f : HalfLine, ∀ᵐ x : ℝ ∂halfLineMeasure,
      Integrable (fun y : ℝ => k (x, y) * f y) halfLineMeasure ∧
      rho.val f x = ∫ y, k (x, y) * f y ∂halfLineMeasure

/-- PDF pp.11–12: r=min(x,y), v=x-y parametrize each characteristic from its boundary. -/
def characteristicPoint (v r : ℝ) : ℝ × ℝ := (r + max v 0, r + max (-v) 0)

/-- PDF pp.3,6–7, Proposition 1: local characteristic AC and its actual weak derivative.
There is no zero boundary condition. The parameter v ranges over the whole real line. -/
def CharacteristicFirst (rho sigma : (TraceClass HalfLine)) : Prop :=
  ∃ k q : ℝ × ℝ → ℂ, HasKernel rho k ∧ HasKernel sigma q ∧
    (∀ᵐ v : ℝ ∂volume,
      LocallyAC (fun r => k (characteristicPoint v r)) ∧
      (∀ᵐ r : ℝ ∂halfLineMeasure,
        HasDerivAt (fun s => k (characteristicPoint v s))
          (q (characteristicPoint v r)) r))

/-- PDF pp.13–14, Proposition 9, corrected using its proof: zero at r=0 on each
characteristic, rather than zero at every interior point. No zero first-derivative
boundary condition is imposed. Both regularity clauses are local. -/
def CharacteristicSecond (rho sigma : (TraceClass HalfLine)) : Prop :=
  ∃ k q : ℝ × ℝ → ℂ, HasKernel rho k ∧ HasKernel sigma q ∧
    (∀ᵐ v : ℝ ∂volume, ∃ d : ℝ → ℂ,
      LocallyAC (fun r => k (characteristicPoint v r)) ∧
      k (characteristicPoint v 0) = 0 ∧ LocallyAC d ∧
      (∀ r : ℝ, 0 ≤ r →
        HasDerivWithinAt (fun s => k (characteristicPoint v s)) (d r) (Set.Ici 0) r) ∧
      (∀ᵐ r : ℝ ∂halfLineMeasure,
        HasDerivAt d (q (characteristicPoint v r)) r))

/-- PDF p.4: an arbitrary countable rebound factorization; zero padding is permitted. -/
def IsReboundDecomposition (b : HilbertBasis ℕ ℂ HalfLine) (Omega : State b)
    (l : ℕ → HalfLine) : Prop :=
  Summable (fun j => ‖l j‖ ^ 2) ∧
  ∀ f : HalfLine, Omega.val.val f = ∑' j, inner ℂ (l j) f • l j

/-- PDF p.4: the actual, possibly nonclosable, H1 boundary-jump graph in L2 times L2. -/
def boundaryJumpGraph (l : HalfLine) : Set (HalfLine × HalfLine) :=
  {z | ∃ df a, H1Trace z.1 df a ∧ z.2 = a • l}

/-- PDF p.4: nonclosability means that the graph closure is not single-valued at zero. -/
def IsNonclosableGraph (G : Set (HalfLine × HalfLine)) : Prop :=
  ∃ y : HalfLine, y ≠ 0 ∧ (0, y) ∈ closure G

/-- PDF p.12, (30): the reflected heat weight is a DIFFERENCE, with squared absolute values. -/
def reflectedWeight (t r xi : ℝ) : ℝ :=
  Real.exp (-|r - xi| ^ 2 / (4 * t)) - Real.exp (-|r + xi| ^ 2 / (4 * t))

/-- PDF p.12, (30): used only for t>0, with integrability separately asserted. -/
def heatKernel (t : ℝ) (k : ℝ × ℝ → ℂ) (p : ℝ × ℝ) : ℂ :=
  ((1 / (2 * Real.sqrt (Real.pi * t)) : ℝ) : ℂ) *
    ∫ xi, (reflectedWeight t (min p.1 p.2) xi : ℂ) *
      k (xi + max (p.1 - p.2) 0, xi + max (p.2 - p.1) 0) ∂halfLineMeasure

/-- PDF pp.11–13: trace-norm continuity of a full complex trace-class trajectory. -/
def TracePathContinuous (rho : NNReal → (TraceClass HalfLine)) : Prop :=
  ∀ t : NNReal,
    Tendsto (fun s : NNReal => traceNormValue ((rho s).val - (rho t).val))
      (nhds t) (nhds 0)

/-- PDF pp.11–13, (27): the weak forward Cauchy problem on every Dirichlet H2 test pair,
including the prescribed initial datum. There is no positivity restriction on the datum. -/
def WeakForwardCauchy (rho : NNReal → (TraceClass HalfLine)) (rhoInitial : (TraceClass HalfLine)) : Prop :=
  rho 0 = rhoInitial ∧ TracePathContinuous rho ∧
  ∀ (f df ddf g dg ddg : HalfLine),
    DirichletTriple f df ddf → DirichletTriple g dg ddg → ∀ t : NNReal,
    HasDerivWithinAt (fun s : ℝ => inner ℂ f ((rho s.toNNReal).val g))
      (2 * inner ℂ df ((rho t).val dg) + inner ℂ ddf ((rho t).val g) +
        inner ℂ f ((rho t).val ddg)) (Set.Ici 0) (t : ℝ)

/-- PDF pp.11–13: the positive time/interior characteristic region. -/
def heatRegion : Set (ℝ × ℝ) := {p | 0 < p.1 ∧ 0 < p.2}

/-- PDF pp.11–13, (29): classical heat regularity in (t,r) on one characteristic.
Here r=(u-|v|)/2, so the equation dt=ddr is exactly partial_t=4 partial_u².
No regularity in the transverse parameter v is required. -/
def ClassicalHeatSection (F : ℝ → ℝ → ℂ) : Prop :=
  ∃ dt dr ddr : ℝ → ℝ → ℂ,
    ContinuousOn (fun p : ℝ × ℝ => F p.1 p.2) heatRegion ∧
    ContinuousOn (fun p : ℝ × ℝ => dt p.1 p.2) heatRegion ∧
    ContinuousOn (fun p : ℝ × ℝ => dr p.1 p.2) heatRegion ∧
    ContinuousOn (fun p : ℝ × ℝ => ddr p.1 p.2) heatRegion ∧
    (∀ t : ℝ, 0 < t → ∀ r : ℝ, 0 < r →
      HasDerivAt (fun s => F s r) (dt t r) t ∧
      HasDerivAt (fun s => F t s) (dr t r) r ∧
      HasDerivAt (fun s => dr t s) (ddr t r) r ∧ dt t r = ddr t r) ∧
    (∀ t : ℝ, 0 < t →
      ContinuousWithinAt (fun r => F t r) (Set.Ici 0) 0 ∧ F t 0 = 0)

/-- PDF pp.12–13, Proposition 8: a jointly measurable kernel version, classical along
almost every characteristic, with the same trace-norm initial condition. All operator
kernel actions carry their integrability conditions through HasKernel. -/
def HeatCauchy (rho : NNReal → (TraceClass HalfLine)) (rhoInitial : (TraceClass HalfLine)) : Prop :=
  rho 0 = rhoInitial ∧ TracePathContinuous rho ∧
  ∃ k : ℝ → ℝ → ℝ → ℂ,
    AEStronglyMeasurable (fun z : ℝ × (ℝ × ℝ) => k z.1 z.2.1 z.2.2)
      (halfLineMeasure.prod (volume.prod halfLineMeasure)) ∧
    (∀ t : NNReal, HasKernel (rho t)
      (fun p => k (t : ℝ) (p.1 - p.2) (min p.1 p.2))) ∧
    (∀ᵐ v : ℝ ∂volume, ClassicalHeatSection (fun t r => k t v r))

/-- Zero belongs to the full H1 graph, with boundary trace zero. -/
example : H1Trace (0 : HalfLine) 0 0 := by
  have hAC : LocallyAC (fun _ : ℝ => (0 : ℂ)) := by
    intro R hR
    exact (contDiff_const : ContDiff ℝ 1 (fun _ : ℝ => (0 : ℂ))).contDiffOn.absolutelyContinuousOnInterval
  refine ⟨fun _ => 0, ?_, hAC, rfl, ?_⟩
  · exact (Lp.coeFn_zero ℂ 2 halfLineMeasure).symm
  · filter_upwards [Lp.coeFn_zero ℂ 2 halfLineMeasure] with x hx
    rw [hx]
    exact hasDerivAt_const x (0 : ℂ)

/-- The zero Dirichlet test is allowed; no normalization is imposed on test vectors. -/
example : DirichletTriple (0 : HalfLine) 0 0 := by
  have hAC : LocallyAC (fun _ : ℝ => (0 : ℂ)) := by
    intro R hR
    exact (contDiff_const : ContDiff ℝ 1 (fun _ : ℝ => (0 : ℂ))).contDiffOn.absolutelyContinuousOnInterval
  refine ⟨fun _ => 0, fun _ => 0, ?_, ?_, rfl, hAC, ?_, ?_⟩
  · exact (Lp.coeFn_zero ℂ 2 halfLineMeasure).symm
  · exact (Lp.coeFn_zero ℂ 2 halfLineMeasure).symm
  · intro x hx
    exact (hasDerivAt_const x (0 : ℂ)).hasDerivWithinAt
  · filter_upwards [Lp.coeFn_zero ℂ 2 halfLineMeasure] with x hx
    rw [hx]
    exact hasDerivAt_const x (0 : ℂ)

/-- The parametrization starts at the correct boundary on the diagonal v=0. -/
example (r : ℝ) : characteristicPoint 0 r = (r, r) := by
  simp [characteristicPoint]

/-- The reflection difference cancels at the absorbing boundary, for every t and xi. -/
example (t xi : ℝ) : reflectedWeight t 0 xi = 0 := by
  simp [reflectedWeight]

/-- Centering a scalar observable uses the actual identity observable. -/
example : identityObservable (0 : HalfLine) = 0 := rfl

/-- A boundary jump with a zero factor has only the zero output; it must not be
included in the printed unqualified nonclosability claim. -/
example (z : HalfLine × HalfLine) (h : z ∈ boundaryJumpGraph 0) : z.2 = 0 := by
  obtain ⟨df, a, ha, hz⟩ := h
  simpa using hz

/-- The characteristic boundary is (v,0) for nonnegative v, not the interior point (x,y). -/
example (v : ℝ) (hv : 0 ≤ v) : characteristicPoint v 0 = (v, 0) := by
  simp [characteristicPoint, max_eq_left hv, max_eq_right (neg_nonpos.mpr hv)]

end QAlgorithms.Papers.Independent.Renew46.P06


